{
  "about": "The catalog of answer views (ADR 264): the components a bot may draw in a ```ui fence of its reply, with their props, lengths, tones, limits and the catalog version each came in (`since`). The server hands it out at GET /api/ui-catalog (`ui-catalog` in `features`); the apps read a fence with one generic validator driven by this file (public/answer-view.js; the shared fixtures are test/fixtures/ui-cases.json). A prop is `{ type, … }`: `string` (max, multiline; empty: an empty one is kept, as a table cell), `number` (min, max, nullable inside a list), `int`, `boolean`, `enum` (values), `tone` (one of `tones`), `https` (a web address), `media` (from: `file` is a path among the bot's files, `https` an image address; exts: the extensions a file may have), `list` (of, max, min) and `object` (props). `required` is a prop that must be there; `counts: \"points\"` adds a list's length to the node's points. A component has `children` (max, only), `in` (the parents it may stand in) and `sourced` (a chart, table or KPI says where its numbers came from). `noReserved` on a string prop (or on the items of a list of strings, as a poll's options): a text that reads as one of the catalog's `reserved` phrases (the owner's words the server reads as an answer, such as the Approve button's: compared in lower case with everything but letters and digits left out) is not read: a prop that is not needed is dropped, one that is needed cuts out its component. `indexes` on an int: a place in the sibling list it names, read as where that item stands among the ones kept. A list whose items stand by position with another's never has a dropped item shift its neighbours: `by` names the list of the same component it is paired with (an item left out of that one is left out here at the same place), `inPlace` keeps an item that can't be read as a blank (an empty text, a null number, an empty list) and, when nothing in the list could be read, cuts the list. A component with a `tile` prop (kpi, gauge, sparkline, chart, table) is bound to a tile of the Board (ADR 264, amendment; ADR 071): `bind` is the path in the tile's data it reads (`value`, `value.used`), a chart's series each have their own `bind` (and the chart's `item` is the field of each row when it is a list of objects, `labelItem` the field that names it), a table's `bind` is its list and each column's `item` the field of a row; the app shows the tile's live values over the written ones, which stay what Copy, notifications and any other reader see. A `source` that only says there is none (`none`, `n/a`, `unknown`, `no source available`, `brak źródła`, read clause by clause: its last clause says so) is no source: it is left out, so the view is flagged `noSource`. Lengths cut, never refuse; only `limits` refuse a fence.",
  "version": 4,
  "limits": { "fences": 3, "nodes": 200, "depth": 6, "bytes": 65536, "points": 500, "alt": 200 },
  "tones": ["neutral", "good", "warn", "bad", "accent"],
  "reserved": ["Approved. Go ahead.", "Build it."],
  "components": {
    "stack": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "Its children one under the other.",
      "props": { "gap": { "type": "enum", "values": ["s", "m", "l"], "default": "m" } },
      "children": { "max": 30 } },
    "row": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "Its children side by side; on a narrow screen one under the other.",
      "props": { "gap": { "type": "enum", "values": ["s", "m", "l"], "default": "m" } },
      "children": { "max": 8 } },
    "grid": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "Its children in 1 to 4 equal columns.",
      "props": { "columns": { "type": "int", "min": 1, "max": 4, "default": 2 }, "gap": { "type": "enum", "values": ["s", "m", "l"], "default": "m" } },
      "children": { "max": 12 } },
    "card": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "A box around its children, with an optional title.",
      "props": { "title": { "type": "string", "max": 80 }, "tone": { "type": "tone", "default": "neutral" } },
      "children": { "max": 20 } },
    "section": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "A titled part of the view, with a one-line lead.",
      "props": { "title": { "type": "string", "max": 80, "required": true }, "lead": { "type": "string", "max": 200 } },
      "children": { "max": 20 } },
    "tabs": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "Its tabs, one shown at a time.",
      "props": {},
      "children": { "max": 6, "only": ["tab"] } },
    "tab": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "One tab of tabs.", "in": ["tabs"],
      "props": { "label": { "type": "string", "max": 30, "required": true } },
      "children": { "max": 20 } },
    "accordion": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "Its panels, each opened and closed on its own.",
      "props": {},
      "children": { "max": 12, "only": ["panel"] } },
    "panel": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "One panel of an accordion.", "in": ["accordion"],
      "props": { "title": { "type": "string", "max": 80, "required": true }, "open": { "type": "boolean" } },
      "children": { "max": 20 } },
    "divider": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "A thin line between parts, with an optional word on it.",
      "props": { "label": { "type": "string", "max": 40 } } },
    "spacer": { "group": "layout", "since": 1, "means": "An empty space.",
      "props": { "size": { "type": "enum", "values": ["s", "m", "l"], "default": "m" } } },

    "heading": { "group": "text", "since": 1, "means": "A heading.",
